# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Scaffolded by `cargo kindle new mnist` -- a minimal Kindle training loop with
telemetry pre-wired.

## Quickstart

```bash
cargo run
```

In another terminal, watch loss live (no browser, no Python):

```bash
cargo kindle watch --run-id <the run id printed on startup>
```

## Next steps

- `src/main.rs` trains on synthetic random data so it runs immediately. Swap
  in real MNIST by following kindle's own
  `crates/kindle/examples/mnist_training.rs` (loads
  `kindle_data::vision::mnist::MnistDataset`).
- Add more `reporter.scalar(...)` / `reporter.gradient_norm(...)` calls
  (see `kindle_telemetry::reporter::Reporter`) to track anything else you
  care about -- they show up in `cargo kindle watch` automatically.
